("premiere",None,"La Bohème premiered on 1 February 1896 at the Teatro Regio in Turin, conducted by the 28-year-old Arturo Toscanini.","conducted by the 28-year-old Arturo Toscanini"),
("premiere",None,"The first-night audience was subdued, and the critics were divided.","The initial response of the audience at the first performance was subdued and critical responses were polarized.","Initial_success"),
("history",None,"Toscanini conducted it again on radio in 1946, 50 years after the premiere. It is the only recording of a Puccini opera by its original conductor.",["In 1946, 50 years after the opera's premiere, Toscanini conducted a commemorative performance","It is the only recording ever made of a Puccini opera by its original conductor."]),
("composer",None,"Ruggero Leoncavallo claimed he had offered Puccini a finished Bohème libretto. Puccini said he hadn't known and wouldn't abandon his own opera, so Leoncavallo wrote a rival Bohème.",["who said that he had offered Puccini a completed libretto","he felt that he could not oblige him by abandoning the opera"],"Origin_of_the_story"),
("history",None,"Leoncavallo\u2019s rival version swapped the voices: his Marcello is a tenor and his Rodolfo a baritone.","Leoncavallo completed his own version in which Marcello was sung by a tenor and Rodolfo by a baritone.","Origin_of_the_story"),
("music","Che gelida manina","\u201cChe gelida manina\u201d was recorded by nearly 500 tenors in at least seven languages between 1900 and 1980.","This aria has been recorded by nearly 500 tenors in at least seven different languages between 1900 and 1980.","Recording_history"),
("artist","Che gelida manina","Enrico Caruso, closely associated with Rodolfo, recorded this aria in 1906.","Enrico Caruso, who was closely associated with the role of Rodolfo, recorded the famous aria \"Che gelida manina\" in 1906.","Recording_history"),
("music","O soave fanciulla","Rodolfo turns to see Mim\u00ec bathed in moonlight, and their voices join in \u201cO soave fanciulla\u201d.","He answers and turns to see Mimì bathed in moonlight (duet, Rodolfo and Mimì: O soave fanciulla","Act_1"),
("music","Aranci, datteri|Act II","Act II opens at the Caf\u00e9 Momus with a big crowd, children included, and street sellers calling out their wares.","A great crowd, including children, has gathered with street sellers announcing their wares","Act_2"),
("music","Addio dolce svegliare|Dunque.*vero","In this quartet, Mim\u00ec and Rodolfo part tenderly while Marcello and Musetta quarrel fiercely about her flirting.","the couple quarrel fiercely about Musetta's flirtatiousness","Act_3"),
("music","O Mim\u00ec, tu pi\u00f9|O Mimi, tu piu","\u201cO Mim\u00ec, tu pi\u00f9 non torni\u201d: Rodolfo and Marcello, both alone again, are nostalgic for their lost loves.","The men both express their nostalgia (duet: O Mimì, tu più non torni","Act_4"),
("history","Sono andati","When news of Puccini\u2019s death reached Rome in 1924, a Bohème performance was stopped and the orchestra played Chopin\u2019s Funeral March.",["the news of his death reached Rome during a performance of La bohème","The opera was immediately stopped, and the orchestra played Chopin's Funeral March for the stunned audience."]),
("history",None,"The Met first staged La Bohème on 26 December 1900, with Nellie Melba as Mim\u00ec.","The Metropolitan Opera staged the work for the first time on 26 December 1900 with Nellie Melba as Mimì"),
